  "_comment": [
    "Cardinal plural category per locale for a numeric argument. Source: CLDR plural rules (SPEC.md, section Plurals); no port ships its own rules. `n` is a decimal string with no visible trailing zeros, so the CLDR operands v and f are 0 and the vectors do not depend on how a port parses numbers.",
    "Values are stable across CLDR 42 and later. Locales are chosen to cover every category and the common edge shapes; a port MAY check more."
  ],
